            B[i, j] = alpha * B[i, j]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optimization schedule
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We apply Exo scheduling primitives to improve locality and expose
# vectorization opportunities along the j dimension (contiguous in memory).
# The two j-loops (one in the update, one in the scaling) are tiled and
# their inner tiles are unrolled. This keeps the mathematical
# computation identical while improving the generated C code.

# Tile size along the j (column) dimension. This is a tuning parameter:
# 32 is a reasonable default for modern cache lines and vector widths.
